<article class="env-lemma" id="02UV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02UV">Lemma <span data-tag="02UV">20.20.1</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of topological spaces. For any abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $Z$ we have $H^ p(Z, \mathcal{F}) = H^ p(X, i_*\mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $i_*$ is exact (see Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01AX" data-tag="01AX">17.6.1</a>), and hence $R^ pi_* = 0$ as a functor (Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015F" data-tag="015F">13.16.9</a>). Thus we may apply Lemma <a href="/tag/01F4" data-tag="01F4">20.13.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>